# Stage 1 — one dependable research loop

[Package home](../README.md) · [Full build plan](05-build-and-done.md) · [Machine exit criteria](../3-agent-reference/stage-1.json)

**This is the first implementation target for every coding agent. Complete its exit criteria before starting the remaining build waves.** Stage 1 makes the portable capsule core useful through native JiuwenSwarm, with a real checked artifact delivery. Passing it permits continuation; it does not mean M2a is complete.

![Stage 1 before the remaining build](../diagrams/06-build.svg)

## The demonstration to build

Give the native JiuwenSwarm agent a small local numerical dataset and a structured research request: compute a specified summary and deliver a report supported by the calculation. Supply a prepared, versioned acceptance contract so building the intent and contract compilers is not on the critical path.

Install two category capsules: **calculation**, exposing `calculate` and `normalize_table`, and **reporting**, exposing `markdown_report`. The agent selects compatible members using a simple declared-contract filter. It chooses whether normalization is needed and can repair a failed call within the bound budget. Do not hard-code a global normalize → calculate → report workflow. Use a clean dataset and a variant needing supported normalization to show different action choices.

Produce actual `result.json`, `report.md`, `manifest.json`, call/check receipts and reproduction instructions. Every numeric claim in the report must match checked calculation evidence. A deterministic independent fixture oracle checks the answer; a real model-backed native agent drives the workflow. Mocked orchestration does not satisfy this demonstration.

## Build only what this slice needs

1. Load immutable category/member declarations, pins and a durable admission record for this local environment. Use real qualification fixtures; no caller-controlled bypass.
2. Implement one guarded invocation path with actual input validation, effect limits, bound required checks, budgets, named errors and receipts. Bind it through Python, CLI, MCP and native JiuwenSwarm tools.
3. Supply a small local artifact provider and trusted calculation/report checks. Store sealed output bytes and receipts before publishing the accepted manifest. No private research pipeline imports or fabricated stage context.
4. Add a minimal durable project/call journal. Exercise restart at the receipt-to-publication boundary: recover the same checked delivery without losing evidence or publishing unchecked output.
5. Run the positive, rejection, repair, portability and restart scenarios below. Record evidence against the Stage 1 IDs.

This is the concrete exit definition of the previous Wave A, with the minimum discovery and restart behavior needed to prove a useful vertical slice. Reuse native agent/session/tool mechanisms. A local transactional store, ordinary files and deterministic filtering are sufficient.

## Stage 1 exit criteria

| ID | Required proof |
|---|---|
| S1-01 | Both category packages and all three members execute in a clean external environment without AI4R research internals. Dependencies and checks are explicit. |
| S1-02 | Python, CLI, MCP and the native binding use the same guarded path. Wrong input, forbidden effects and missing/failed required checks cannot produce accepted output. |
| S1-03 | A real JiuwenSwarm agent completes the clean and normalization-needed tasks; observed traces show input-dependent choice, checked results and the declared budget. |
| S1-04 | An injected repairable failure produces a named rejection and bounded correction or alternative. Persist both attempts; reject unsupported values rather than inventing them. |
| S1-05 | A real delivery contains the result, evidence-linked report, manifest, receipts and reproduction instructions. Independent recomputation matches the accepted result. |
| S1-06 | Restart between durable receipt and manifest publication recovers exactly one accepted delivery; missing or changed output bytes prevent publication. |
| S1-07 | Record exact code/environment/model/checker pins, runnable commands and observed results for all six preceding criteria. A reviewer can rerun the deterministic checks and inspect the native traces. |

All seven must PASS. A named rejection can satisfy a negative test, but cannot substitute for the successful positive demonstration. Only actual results update runtime status; design fixtures and schemas are not evidence that Stage 1 works. [Stage 1 status](../3-agent-reference/implementation-status.json) starts at NOT_RUN.

## After Stage 1

Continue to Wave B (intent, contract, literature and richer research revision), then Wave C (all remaining members, durable asynchronous jobs and complete delivery), then Wave D (full fault qualification and matched research trials). The full M2A obligations remain open until independently proven across their complete scope.

Defer learned/vector routing, the other capsule members, factory/RSI automation, general-purpose remote execution, the 24-hour run and the 36-run comparison to their existing later milestones. Stage 1 proves a small local slice, not unattended long-run reliability or scientific superiority. Do not add these deferred features before the Stage 1 exit unless a concrete failing exit criterion requires the dependency.
